1200 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Richard: So, here's the thing. We've received a flood of preorders for\your next song, even though we haven't announced a release yet. You\wouldn't think it was mentioned in the newspaper only yesterday...":GOSUB 5100:BM$="At any rate, we must figure something out for the recording.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1210 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Andrew: How about we record tonight's live? We'll just have to cut the\part with the new song and bam, `live version`.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1220 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Alan: A live version would definitely be quick to release, though I don't\think it would convey the right feeling of the song... What do you think,\Martin?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1230 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Martin: Well, it's already all over the press, so there's no time for a studio\recording. I say we go for the live version, and record a studio version\once the holidays are over.":GOSUB 5100
1231 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Alan: Yeah, I like that. I always wanted to record multiple versions of it\anyway. Starting with a live version is definitely unique.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1240 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Richard: Releasing a live version first, hmmm? It could work, considering\how good David is now. Okay, that settles it!":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1250 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: Then we'll have to give tonight's concert some extra oomph. I want\Martin's new song to be memorable.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1260 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: Don't go overboard with the oomph, David. If the crowd gets too\crazy we won't be able to get a good recording.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1270 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Martin: She's right, you know. I don't want it to be just a bonus track\because there's too many screams to be serviceable.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1280 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Richard: You can stay at the hotel after the concert. All expenses are\already covered.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1290 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Andrew: I'll go back to my room and figure out how I can spend my holiday.\See you tomorrow night.":GOSUB 5100
1295 BM$="Each member of the band were renting rooms in different apartments in\the city. They decided to leave the hotel the following day and return to\their own homes.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1300 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Richard: You live in London so you should be fine, but what about your\holiday, Susanna?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1310 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: I was thinking of leaving the city and relaxing in the countryside\for a while.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1320 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Richard: Sounds good. Meanwhile, I won't be able to rest at all thanks to you\guys. In fact, I'd better get going... See you tonight.":GOSUB 5100
1330 GOSUB 9535:WEND PR:BM$="President Richard and Susanna left. David and the others decided to go\to the lobby for a cup of coffee.":GOSUB 5000
1335 COMMON FO:GOSUB 9540:GOSUB 9520:GOSUB 9510
1340 GOSUB 9010:GOSUB 9515:GOSUB 6120:BM$="The sun was setting. The last concert of the European Tour would be held\at the Royal Albert Hall.":GOSUB 5100:'
1350 BM$="Outside, the venue was surrounded by a record number of fans.":GOSUB 5100
1360 GOSUB 9525:GOSUB 6110:BM$="Inside the hall, the crowd's cheers turned into screams more and more,\with each song. Once again, it was a frenzy. David held out his hand to the\audience, to calm it down.":GOSUB 5100
1370 GOSUB 6160:ISET X:COMMON FO:BM$="David: This is what you've all been waiting for. Our newest song, written by\Martin during our tour of Europe... PRAYERS!":GOSUB 5100
1380 GOSUB 9020:GOSUB 6230:BM$="The crowd erupted in cheers.":GOSUB 5100:'
1390 GOSUB 6110:BM$="Andrew started clapping slowly, and the intro of the song began to play. It\was a calm, quiet flow. For a moment, it was as if the venue had been\submerged underwater.":GOSUB 5100
1395 BM$="The crowd was surprised by this song. It was different from anything\Eleno Vision had ever played."
1400 GOSUB 6280:BM$="Martin's sampler played some light drums, which merged with Alan's\ambient synth, echoing throughout the hall.":GOSUB 5100
1410 GOSUB 6290:BM$="David took the microphone, and let the rhythm enter his body. The\audience started clapping slowly, following the beat set by Andrew.":GOSUB 5100
1430 GOSUB 6200:BM$="Once Alan backed them with the piano, the audience went wild.":GOSUB 5100
1440 GOSUB 6170:BM$="David started singing with every ounce of energy he had in his body.":GOSUB 5100
1445 GOSUB 6220:BM$="The band was surprised at how well their song was being received, pleased\that they were being appreciated even with such a different image.":GOSUB 5100
1450 GOSUB 6240:BM$="The crowd - or rather, everyone in the venue - started dancing, as in a\frenzy.":GOSUB 5100
1470 GOSUB 6295:BM$="Once David finished singing, the audience went silent. Not a single clap\could be heard.":GOSUB 5100
1480 GOSUB 6160:BM$="David: It's over.":GOSUB 5100
1490 GOSUB 6230:BM$="As if they had been released from some sort of hypnosis, they started\clapping and cheering.":GOSUB 5100
1500 GOSUB 6210:BM$="Martin was delighted, waving his hands to the crowd.":GOSUB 5100
1510 COMMON FO:GOSUB 6110:BM$="After giving their encore, the curtains lowered on Eleno Vision's tour of\Europe.":GOSUB 5100
1515 GOSUB 6250:BM$="Once the frenzy had passed, the staff thought it was a miracle that no\incidents had happened, some even making the sign of the cross on their\chest.":GOSUB 5100
1520 BM$="After the concert, the band got ready for the closing party that\President Richard had been preparing. It was usually a small, intimate\event, but not this time.":GOSUB 5100
1530 GOSUB 9030:GOSUB 6130:BM$="David and the others returned to the hotel, changed their clothes, and\entered the party hall on the third floor.":GOSUB 5100:'
1540 BM$="They were greeted by politicians, businessmen, and members of the press.\President Richard told them he had a hard time narrowing down the\guests.":GOSUB 5100
1550 BM$="Once the party was in full swing, the front desk clerk approached David\with a sealed letter. He opened the envelope, and read its contents.":GOSUB 5100
1560 GOSUB 6140:BM$="`I have precise information about the Devil King. Come to Cafe Alice\(between Westminster Bridge and Westminster Abbey) tomorrow at noon,\alone. Don't tell anyone.`":GOSUB 5100
1570 BM$="David read the letter over and over. He felt the blood drain from his face.\How could anyone else know about the Devil King? About his nightmares?":GOSUB 5100
1580 GOSUB 6135:BM$="The party ended after 2am. Still tired from the concert, the band\returned to their personal rooms. With the protagonists gone, the guests\began to leave as well.":GOSUB 5100
